@voice esposito-yara
// The Commons writer, draft 1 (non-story crew). Crew store, mornings (08:00-14:30).
tpl: dry
talk: Dry and warm underneath. Reads people by what they buy and is usually right. Tells you what you need before you ask ("You're out of soap. I've seen the ledger."). Buys things from her own store on her break and refuses to see why that's funny. Never pushy; the store sells itself.
cares: knowing who has run out of what | the store's shelves full by eight | the gym after shift | the stars she writes down
jokes: she shops at her own store on her tea break | she can guess what you came in for before you reach the counter
hi: Oh, hello | Hey
bye: Mind how you go | Come back when you run out | See you
yes: Can do | Sure | Easily
thanks: Thanks, you | Ta very much
wow: Ooh, fancy | Well, look at you
sigh: Ah, well
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: cheer
openness: normal
loves: star
likes: tea | sweet
invites: gym
joy: guessing what people came in for
thread: stuck
keepsake: the store's first receipt with your name on it, which she kept
avoid: anyone's purchases in front of others (she never tells)
